From 543e9f1f83caa52e6479e958ce753098c00d8642 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:46:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(wire): allow sharp inside corners at the wire radius

A Wire Contour gets the per-operation option sharp_corners (default off).
When it is on, the cover law accepts an uncut inside-corner rest up to
the kerf offset (wire radius + spark gap). The worst rest is said as a
note on the path and on the post's wire verify line. It is not a
refusal. A rest past the kerf offset stays refused, with a message that
says the option was on. Off keeps today's refusal.

The key rides the project file (absent when off), the wire page
(Geometry tab checkbox, applied by EditOperationParams) and MCP
edit_operation through the params DTO.

Fixes #3207

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
